question:
Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies the following system of congruences:

\[
\begin{cases}
x^2 \equiv 1 \pmod{7} \\
x^2 \equiv 4 \pmod{11} \\
x^2 \equiv 9 \pmod{13}
\end{cases}
\]

Find the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies the following system of congruences:
\[
\begin{cases}
x \equiv 2 \pmod{3} \\
x \equiv 3 \pmod{5} \\
x \equiv 2 \pmod{7}
\end{cases}
\]

What is the smallest positive integer \( x \) that satisfies both of the following congruences?
\[
\begin{align*}
x &\equiv 3 \pmod{7} \\
x &\equiv 5 \pmod{11}
\end{align*}
\]
